{"id": "money-the-ledger-stops-following", "title": "Stipends through a bank, gift cards, intermediaries: money the ledger stops following", "seconds": 130.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.055, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "2ba5f35f85226657", "words": 349, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "Who gets the stipends San Francisco pays people in its programs?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.5, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Stipends", "sub": "small payments to people in City programs"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.46, 0.57, 1.16, 1.4, 1.96, 2.31, 2.66, 2.76, 2.94]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The biggest payee isn’t a person. It’s a bank, US Bank. How much?", "t0": 4.5, "t1": 10.23, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The largest payee", "sub": "the City’s “Stipends” account"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.6, 1.08, 1.32, 1.39, 2.38, 2.64, 2.72, 3.44, 3.84, 4.84, 5.09]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "oneLine"], "text": "7.7 million dollars.", "t0": 10.23, "t1": 12.23, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$7.7 million", "label": "stipends paid to US Bank National Association", "sub": "$7.1 million from Economic & Workforce Development, fiscal 2021 to 2025"}, "emph": ["7.7"], "wt": [0.04, 0.4, 0.7, 1.01, 1.38]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 12.75, "t1": 14.38, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.34, 0.43, 0.79, 0.98, 1.06]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "A bank can pay many people at once.", "t0": 14.5, "t1": 16.52, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Economic & Workforce Development", "sub": "stipends"}, {"art": "money", "name": "US Bank National Association", "sub": "the payee on file"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Who received them?", "sub": "how many people, in what form: not in the file"}], "kicker": "Where the trail ends"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.46, 0.63, 0.84, 1.07, 1.4, 1.55]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "But then the file shows only the bank. Not who, or how many.", "t0": 16.64, "t1": 20.32, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Economic & Workforce Development", "sub": "stipends"}, {"art": "money", "name": "US Bank National Association", "sub": "the payee on file"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Who received them?", "sub": "how many people, in what form: not in the file"}], "kicker": "Where the trail ends"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.31, 0.42, 0.76, 1.09, 1.43, 1.54, 2.18, 2.49, 2.88, 3.12, 3.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The Police Department used the same route:", "t0": 20.44, "t1": 22.54, "shot": "b4p", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Police Department", "sub": "$516,498 in stipends paid to the bank, fiscal 2024 to 2026; no contract number"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 0.95, 1.15, 1.26, 1.54]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "516,498 dollars, with no contract number on file.", "t0": 22.54, "t1": 28.03, "shot": "b4p", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Police Department", "sub": "$516,498 in stipends paid to the bank, fiscal 2024 to 2026; no contract number"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.41, 0.8, 1.32, 1.81, 2.1, 2.45, 2.99, 3.54, 3.8, 4.05, 4.59, 4.89, 5.05]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why", "established[0]"], "text": "Next, gift cards: cash, once they leave the drawer.", "t0": 28.25, "t1": 31.33, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.83, 1.38, 1.93, 2.19, 2.35, 2.57, 2.66]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why", "established[0]"], "text": "Three Controller audits found records too thin to account for every card.", "t0": 31.45, "t1": 35.44, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "emph": ["too thin"], "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.86, 1.28, 1.55, 1.99, 2.26, 2.58, 2.71, 3.1, 3.26, 3.55]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Human Services bought 2.8 million dollars of cards.", "t0": 35.56, "t1": 38.93, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.86, 1.12, 1.35, 1.64, 1.89, 2.25, 2.63, 2.74]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "One program used 1 of the 500 it got.", "t0": 39.05, "t1": 41.56, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "emph": ["1 of the 500"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.78, 0.97, 1.12, 1.21, 1.32, 1.61, 1.97, 2.09]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "At the Human Rights Commission, 20,507 dollars of cards had no proof of purchase.", "t0": 41.68, "t1": 47.68, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.3, 0.6, 0.89, 1.48, 1.89, 2.39, 2.73, 3.12, 3.47, 3.86, 3.97, 4.42, 4.63, 4.85, 5.18, 5.31]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[1]", "next[4]"], "text": "And purchase codes miss prepaid debit cards, like Visa ReliaCards. So the full total isn’t known.", "t0": 47.8, "t1": 54.31, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Visa ReliaCards, which are prepaid debit cards"}, "emph": ["isn’t known"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.58, 0.97, 1.21, 1.71, 1.99, 2.65, 2.9, 3.2, 4.82, 5.03, 5.12, 5.41, 5.82, 6.1]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Then, intermediaries: contracts that pay someone to pass money on.", "t0": 54.53, "t1": 59.73, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City department", "sub": "pays"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Fiscal intermediary, agent or sponsor", "sub": "paid to pass money on"}, {"art": "question", "name": "People or a named project", "sub": "not in the payment file"}], "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 2.23, 2.86, 3.05, 3.31, 3.63, 3.72, 4.03, 4.34]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "How much since 2019?", "t0": 59.73, "t1": 62.21, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City department", "sub": "pays"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Fiscal intermediary, agent or sponsor", "sub": "paid to pass money on"}, {"art": "question", "name": "People or a named project", "sub": "not in the payment file"}], "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.59, 0.89, 1.23]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "amount"], "text": "111.5 million dollars.", "t0": 62.21, "t1": 64.92, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$111.5 million", "label": "paid since fiscal 2019 to 19 payees"}, "emph": ["111.5"], "wt": [0.04, 0.29, 0.64, 1.03, 1.33, 1.68, 2.08]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Healthright 360 alone got 77.7 million. The record ends there.", "t0": 65.44, "t1": 71.13, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to pass money on, since fiscal 2019", "rows": [["Healthright 360 · fiscal intermediary", "$77.7 million"], ["Abode Services · fiscal agent", "$11.4 million"], ["Community Initiatives · fiscal sponsor", "$7.8 million"], ["San Francisco Study Center Inc", "$5.5 million"]]}, "emph": ["77.7 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.49, 0.74, 1.06, 1.47, 1.87, 2.09, 2.81, 3.11, 3.41, 4.32, 4.52, 4.9, 5.25]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Community benefit districts are funded by assessments on their own property owners.", "t0": 71.35, "t1": 75.81, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Community benefit districts", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "funded by assessments on their own property owners"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.97, 1.47, 1.64, 1.99, 2.15, 2.79, 2.94, 3.15, 3.38, 3.89]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Yet in 5, City grants came to half that or more.", "t0": 75.93, "t1": 78.92, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Excelsior Action Group", "City grants: 205% of its assessment"], "b": ["Noe Valley Association", "55%"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.39, 0.86, 1.17, 1.57, 1.82, 1.95, 2.23, 2.46, 2.6]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Excelsior Action Group: 205 percent.", "t0": 79.04, "t1": 81.71, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Excelsior Action Group", "City grants: 205% of its assessment"], "b": ["Noe Valley Association", "55%"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, "emph": ["205 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.92, 1.25, 1.47, 1.84, 2.13]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "City grantees, with boards the City doesn’t appoint.", "t0": 81.83, "t1": 84.79, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Excelsior Action Group", "City grants: 205% of its assessment"], "b": ["Noe Valley Association", "55%"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 1.04, 1.25, 1.69, 1.81, 2.12, 2.44]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[8]"], "text": "Lower Polk’s district paid 1.4 million dollars to a firm run by its former executive director.", "t0": 84.91, "t1": 90.77, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Lower Polk Community Benefit District", "sub": "cleaning and ambassador services, 3 returns", "chip": "$1.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.75, 1.27, 1.55, 1.78, 2.08, 2.37, 2.75, 3.19, 3.35, 3.43, 3.75, 4.03, 4.19, 4.38, 4.74, 5.26]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[8]"], "text": "Its own return says so.", "t0": 90.89, "t1": 92.32, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Lower Polk Community Benefit District", "sub": "cleaning and ambassador services, 3 returns", "chip": "$1.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.41, 0.8, 1.07]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Last, rent. The Airport, the Port and the Real Estate Division may forgive rent tenant by tenant.", "t0": 92.54, "t1": 98.99, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The Airport, the Port, the Real Estate Division", "sub": "standing authority"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Rent forgiven or reduced", "sub": "tenant by tenant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "no file"}], "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.73, 1.77, 1.96, 2.64, 2.78, 3.22, 3.41, 3.49, 3.7, 3.97, 4.41, 4.62, 5.06, 5.37, 5.75, 5.94]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Those sums are in no Board file.", "t0": 99.11, "t1": 100.97, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The Airport, the Port, the Real Estate Division", "sub": "standing authority"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Rent forgiven or reduced", "sub": "tenant by tenant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "no file"}], "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.63, 0.79, 0.89, 1.06, 1.38]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The Airport’s own pandemic estimate: 21.8 million dollars. The rest is unknown.", "t0": 101.09, "t1": 107.02, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$21.8 million", "label": "the Airport’s own estimate for its pandemic programme"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.69, 0.97, 1.56, 2.07, 2.7, 3.01, 3.28, 3.68, 4.71, 4.91, 5.24, 5.4]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Two things checked out: charges between departments hold steady, and hospital bad debt is falling.", "t0": 107.24, "t1": 113.39, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["charges between departments", "7.7% of spending, steady"], "b": ["hospital bad debt", "1.3% of gross charges, falling"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.55, 0.9, 1.61, 2.1, 2.43, 2.98, 3.27, 4.03, 4.28, 4.81, 5.12, 5.43, 5.59]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Nothing shows any stipend, card or pass-through payment went to the wrong person.", "t0": 113.61, "t1": 117.92, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any stipend, card or pass-through payment went to the wrong person", "What fee each intermediary kept"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.66, 0.87, 1.61, 1.97, 2.1, 2.64, 3.03, 3.26, 3.35, 3.43, 3.71]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[4]", "next[0]"], "text": "What would settle it? Each department’s gift-card log, and the lists of rent forgiven.", "t0": 118.04, "t1": 122.96, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Each department’s gift-card log: bought, issued, on hand, lost"}, {"who": "", "what": "The Port’s and the Airport’s lists of rent forgiven, tenant by tenant"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.32, 0.67, 1.45, 1.77, 2.36, 2.92, 3.33, 3.48, 3.59, 3.89, 4.04, 4.32]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "On every route, the public record stops before the final recipient.", "t0": 123.08, "t1": 127.04, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.56, 1.01, 1.17, 1.56, 1.93, 2.38, 2.74, 2.85, 3.23]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.16, "t1": 129.35, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.43, 0.54, 0.61, 1.09, 1.29, 1.38]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "Lead 1 · gift cards", "lead2": "Lead 2 · intermediaries", "lead3": "Lead 3 · benefit districts", "lead4": "Lead 4 · rent forgiven", "found": "What checked out", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "question"}